<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Future Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While effective, <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> presents several opportunities for further improvement. One notable limitation is the structural bias towards earlier tokens, a common drawback in many existing cache eviction methods, which also emerges in <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span>, particularly as the perturbation window increase. Although heuristics like retaining a fixed-size recent window help mitigate this bias by leveraging the locality of attention patterns, such strategies remain static and empirically driven. Future work should more systematically investigate the design and adaptability of perturbation windows to better improve saliency estimation. Additionally, <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span>’s current dynamic cache eviction strategy in the decoding phase directly follows H<sub id="A1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O by accumulating saliency scores over time, effectively minimizing perturbations over the full sequence history. However, under our formulation, alternative objectives could be explored. For example, accumulating scores only within a recent attention window. Such variants may yield improved adaptability in long-context generation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the theoretical side, <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> introduces a flexible, perturbation-minimization framework that can be extended to a broader class of KV cache compression strategies. For instance, due to the inherent flexibility of structured pruning, one could adapt the <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> formulation to key channel pruning by redefining the pruning units from tokens to channels. Leveraging approximation techniques, it is possible to derive corresponding closed-form saliency scores from an output-aware perspective, enabling informed channel-level pruning decisions. Moreover, our approach relies on the diagonal Hessian assumption used in Optimal Brain Damage, which supports only token removal. In contrast, another classical pruning theory Optimal Brain Surgeon relaxes this assumption by allowing compensation across pruning units, adjusting remaining parameters to reduce loss. This perspective aligns naturally with recent works on cache merging, and could inspire more theoretically grounded cache management techniques for long-context LLMs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, <span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> offers a flexible foundation for future research into KV cache compression. Its structured and theoretically motivated formulation opens up promising directions for designing more effective and principled KV cache management.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we demonstrate the full proof and derivations to obtain the <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> scores in Equation <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, Equation <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, as well as their reduction to other attention-based scoring methods. We use consistent notations as previously defined in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Preliminaries on LLM Inference ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>OBCache Objective Function</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As demonstrated in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Cache Eviction via Perturbation Minimization ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Connection to Existing Methods ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we formulate the saliency score for a candidate key-value token as Equation <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Cache Eviction via Perturbation Minimization ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, which is the <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pruning-induced eviction error</span> within a <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">perturbation window</span> for query positions <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})\;:=\;\big\|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{w:s}-{\mathbf{O}}_{w:s}\big\|_{F}^{2}\;=\;\big\|\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{Q}}_{w:s}{\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big)\widehat{\mathbf{V}}-\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{Q}}_{w:s}{\mathbf{K}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big){\mathbf{V}}\big\|_{F}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐊</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})\;:=\;\big\|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{w:s}-{\mathbf{O}}_{w:s}\big\|_{F}^{2}\;=\;\big\|\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{Q}}_{w:s}{\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big)\widehat{\mathbf{V}}-\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{Q}}_{w:s}{\mathbf{K}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big){\mathbf{V}}\big\|_{F}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In what follows, we let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}={\mathbf{a}}_{i}{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐎</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}={\mathbf{a}}_{i}{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature element in the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row vector of the attention output matrix <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{a}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{a}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row vector of the attention weight matrix. The squared Frobenius norm objective in Equation <a href="#A2.E11" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> can be explicitly decomposed into a summation form across all element-wise squared error:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}{\mathcal{L}}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})&amp;=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big)\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}-\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{K}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big){\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}|^{2}\\
&amp;\overset{\triangle}{=}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\bm{E}}_{i,j}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">△</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}{\mathcal{L}}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})&amp;=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big)\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}-\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{K}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big){\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}|^{2}\\
&amp;\overset{\triangle}{=}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\bm{E}}_{i,j}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For clarity in the following derivations, we define <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{E}}_{i,j}:=|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{E}}_{i,j}:=|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as the squared difference of the output element <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> before and after applying a perturbation <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding explicitly, the <span id="A2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">element-wise output perturbation</span> for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{E}_{i,j}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})=|\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big)\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}-\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{K}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big){\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{E}_{i,j}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})=|\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big)\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}-\mathrm{softmax}\big({\tfrac{{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{K}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}}\big){\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Given this element-wise objective, we follow the Optimal Brain Damage (OBD) theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">LeCun et al., 1989</a>)</cite> to apply a second-order Taylor expansion of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{E}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{E}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and analytically approximate the element-wise output perturbation:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{E}_{i,j}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})\ \overset{\text{second}}{\underset{\text{order}}{=}}\ \bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>=</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">order</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">second</mtext></munderover><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{E}_{i,j}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})\ \overset{\text{second}}{\underset{\text{order}}{=}}\ \bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\ \delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}\ +\ \dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}^{2}}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\ \delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}\ +\ \dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}^{2}}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\ \delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\ +\ \dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}\delta\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\ \delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\ +\ \dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}\delta\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\ \delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\delta\mathbf{K}\ +\ {\mathcal{O}}(\|(\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j},\delta\mathbf{K})\|^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\ \delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\delta\mathbf{K}\ +\ {\mathcal{O}}(\|(\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j},\delta\mathbf{K})\|^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Through substitution into Equation <a href="#A2.E13" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, the constant term <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes because we have <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> at the expansion point <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the full matrix-wise objective, <span id="A2.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pruning-induced eviction error</span>, approximated via a Taylor-series to the second order, becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})\ \overset{\text{second}}{\underset{\text{order}}{=}}\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>=</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">order</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">second</mtext></munderover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}(\widehat{\mathbf{V}},\widehat{\mathbf{K}})\ \overset{\text{second}}{\underset{\text{order}}{=}}\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}+\dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}^{2}}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}+\dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{V}^{\top}_{:,j}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}^{2}}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}+\dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial{\bm{E}}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}+\dfrac{1}{2}\delta\mathbf{K}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\delta\mathbf{K}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\delta\mathbf{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Isolated Value-Pruning Score</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In isolated value pruning, the key-cache matrix is not perturbed and is considered a constant not affecting <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, minimizing the pruning-induced eviction error reduces to minimizing Equation <a href="#A2.E14" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. To derive saliency scores in closed form, we begin by deriving expressions for the gradient and Hessian with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. The first-order derivative of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{E}}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{E}}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}\hat{{\mathbf{a}}}_{i}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\hat{{\mathbf{a}}}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}\hat{{\mathbf{a}}}_{i}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\hat{{\mathbf{a}}}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When evaluated at <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we again have <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}-{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}-{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the gradient term vanishes to zero. The Hessian of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated at <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}^{2}}=2\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}\Big((\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\hat{{\mathbf{a}}}_{i}^{\top}\Big)\Big(\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}\Big)^{\top}\Bigg|_{({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}=2{\mathbf{a}}_{i}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝑬</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}^{2}}=2\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}\Big((\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\hat{{\mathbf{a}}}_{i}^{\top}\Big)\Big(\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}}\Big)^{\top}\Bigg|_{({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}=2{\mathbf{a}}_{i}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting the gradient and Hessian back into Equation <a href="#A2.E14" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, we get the pruning-induced eviction error when value states are considered as isolate pruning units:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{value}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}({\mathbf{a}}_{i}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i})\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>value</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{value}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}({\mathbf{a}}_{i}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i})\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Next, the row-wise pruning constraint in Equation <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Cache Eviction via Perturbation Minimization ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> implies that when pruning the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th token position, the value cache perturbation <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is explicitly in the form:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{V}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\forall\ j=1,...,d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{V}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\forall\ j=1,...,d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Substituting this value perturbation into <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{value}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>value</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{value}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the output perturbation when pruning the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th value vector from the value cache <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{value}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}|^{2}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}|^{2}=\boxed{\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}\|^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>value</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></menclose></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{value}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}|^{2}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}|^{2}=\boxed{\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}\|^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This is also the value-pruning saliency score for evicting the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th value vector <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{v}}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{v}}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> from the value cache. It is consistent with the expression in Equation <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Isolated Key-Pruning Score</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In isolated key pruning, the value-cache matrix is not perturbed and is assumed a constant. Therefore, minimizing the pruning-induced eviction error reduces to minimizing Equation <a href="#A2.E15" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>. Same as in value-pruning score, we begin by deriving closed-form expressions for the gradient and Hessian with respect to <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The first-order derivative of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{E}}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{E}}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}|\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Before deriving the first-order term explicitly, note that when evaluated at the point <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we again have <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}-{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}-{\mathbf{O}}_{ij}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the first-order term is eliminated, a result that is the same as in isolated value pruning. We now explicitly derive the term <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}:=\tfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}:=\tfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}</annotation></semantics></math> above:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{{\bm{M}}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{{\bm{M}}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\Big)_{p,r}=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\Big)_{p,r}=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}(\dfrac{e^{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,m}}}{\sum_{u=1}^{s}e^{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,u}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}(\dfrac{e^{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,m}}}{\sum_{u=1}^{s}e^{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,u}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}\sum_{u=1}^{s}\dfrac{\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,u}}\dfrac{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,u}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\dfrac{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}\sum_{u=1}^{s}\dfrac{\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}}{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,u}}\dfrac{\widehat{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,u}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\sum_{u=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}(\delta_{mu}-\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,u})\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\delta_{up}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\sum_{u=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}(\delta_{mu}-\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,u})\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\delta_{up}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}(\delta_{mp}-\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p})\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\ \ \ \text{($\delta_{up}=0$ when $u\neq p$)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mtext> when </mtext><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}(\delta_{mp}-\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p})\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\ \ \ \text{($\delta_{up}=0$ when $u\neq p$)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot(\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}\cdot\delta_{mp}-\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot(\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}\cdot\delta_{mp}-\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}-\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m})\ \ \ \text{($\delta_{mp}=0$ when $m\neq p$)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mtext> when </mtext><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}-\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot\sum_{m=1}^{s}\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{m,j}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,m})\ \ \ \text{($\delta_{mp}=0$ when $m\neq p$)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the first-order derivative of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{E}}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{E}}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the perturbed key cache <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)},\text{ where }\widehat{{\bm{M}}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}=2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)},\text{ where }\widehat{{\bm{M}}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now proceed to derive the Hessian, which is a 4-th order tensor of size <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\times d\times s\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\times d\times s\times d</annotation></semantics></math>. The second-order derivative of the element-wise perturbation <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{E}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{E}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}\otimes\left(\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\right)+2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}\otimes\left(\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\right)+2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}\otimes\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}+2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}\otimes\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}+2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\widehat{{\bm{M}}}^{(i,j)}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the matrix-wise outer product<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1</span></span>
              
              
              
            For any two matrices <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{C}},{\bm{D}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{C}},{\bm{D}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the output tensor via outer product is <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times d\times s\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑫</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{C}}\otimes{\bm{D}}\in\mathbb{R}^{s\times d\times s\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>. Since the Hessian will be evaluated at the point <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where the perturbed attention output again matches the original, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the second term in Equation <a href="#A2.E23" title="In B.3 Isolated Key-Pruning Score ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> vanishes. Therefore, the Hessian is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}\Big|_{({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}^{2}}\Big|_{({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}\otimes{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}=2\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})^{\top}\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}\otimes{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}=2\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})^{\top}\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{ where }{\bm{M}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{ where }{\bm{M}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Here, we use <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{vec}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{vec}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the vectorization of a matrix. Substituting the gradient and Hessian back into Equation <a href="#A2.E15" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we get the pruning-induced eviction error when key states are considered as isolate pruning units:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{key}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>key</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{key}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\text{vec}(\delta\mathbf{K})^{\top}\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})^{\top}\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})\text{vec}(\delta\mathbf{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\text{vec}(\delta\mathbf{K})^{\top}\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})^{\top}\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})\text{vec}(\delta\mathbf{K})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})\text{vec}(\delta\mathbf{K})|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\text{vec}({\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})\text{vec}(\delta\mathbf{K})|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the row-wise pruning constraint in Equation <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Cache Eviction via Perturbation Minimization ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> implies that when pruning the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th token position, the key cache perturbation <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is explicitly in the form:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{K}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{K}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\forall\ j=1,...,d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{K}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{K}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\forall\ j=1,...,d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Substituting this key perturbation into <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{key}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>key</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{key}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the output perturbation when pruning the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th value vector from the value cache <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> (we let <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{m}}_{p}^{(i,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{m}}_{p}^{(i,j)}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th row vector of <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{key}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{m}}_{p}^{(i,j)}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>key</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{key}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{m}}_{p}^{(i,j)}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\sum_{r=1}^{d}\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\sum_{r=1}^{d}\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{d}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot\sum_{r=1}^{d}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{d}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot\sum_{r=1}^{d}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}{\mathbf{K}}_{p,r}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{d}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{d}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{d}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\left(|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot|{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top}|^{2}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{d}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\left(|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot|{\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top}|^{2}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}|^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boxed{\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot|{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}-{\mathbf{o}}_{i}\|^{2}_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></menclose></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boxed{\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot|{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,p}|^{2}\cdot\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}-{\mathbf{o}}_{i}\|^{2}_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p">This is also the key-pruning saliency score for evicting the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th key vector <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{k}}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{k}}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> from the key cache. It is consistent with the expression in Equation <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Joint-Pruning Score</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When both <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> are treated as variables affecting <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to compute the cross-term in the error function, which corresponds to deriving a closed-form expression for Equation <a href="#A2.E16" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>. Given that the first-order derivative of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{E}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{E}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is known, we can compute the cross-term as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\hat{\mathbf{a}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\hat{\mathbf{a}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\hat{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\otimes\left(\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\right)+2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\hat{\mathbf{a}}_{i}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐎</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\hat{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\otimes\left(\dfrac{\partial}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\right)+2(\widehat{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\dfrac{\partial\hat{\mathbf{a}}_{i}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Same as in deriving key-pruning scores, the second term above will be zero when evaluated at the point <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the cross second-order term is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\Big|_{({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}=2{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\otimes{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\text{ where }{\bm{M}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext> where </mtext><msubsup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{\partial^{2}\bm{E}_{i,j}}{\partial\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{:,j}\partial\widehat{\mathbf{K}}}\Big|_{({\mathbf{V}}_{:,j},{\mathbf{K}})}=2{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\otimes{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\text{ where }{\bm{M}}_{p,r}^{(i,j)}=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{Q}}_{i,r}\cdot{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting this back into Equation <a href="#A2.E16" title="In B.1 OBCache Objective Function ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, we get the cross-term of the pruning-induced eviction error when the the value and key states are considered as combined pruning units:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}(2{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\otimes{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})\delta\mathbf{K}=2\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}(\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i})\cdot\langle{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\delta\mathbf{K}\rangle_{F}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cross</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}(2{\mathbf{a}}_{i}\otimes{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)})\delta\mathbf{K}=2\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}(\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i})\cdot\langle{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\delta\mathbf{K}\rangle_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\delta\mathbf{K}\rangle_{F}=\sum_{p,r}{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}_{p,r}\cdot\delta\mathbf{K}_{p,r}=\textbf{tr}({{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}}^{\top}\delta\mathbf{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\delta\mathbf{K}\rangle_{F}=\sum_{p,r}{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}_{p,r}\cdot\delta\mathbf{K}_{p,r}=\textbf{tr}({{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)}}^{\top}\delta\mathbf{K})</annotation></semantics></math> is the Frobenius inner product.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When the <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-th key and value are pruned, the row-wise pruning constraint in Equation <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Cache Eviction via Perturbation Minimization ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> implies that the value cache perturbation <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and the key cache perturbation <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are explicitly in the form:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{V}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\delta\mathbf{K}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{K}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\forall\ j=1,...,d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{V}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\delta\mathbf{K}_{t,j}=\begin{cases}-{\mathbf{K}}_{p,j},&amp;\text{when }t=p\\
0,&amp;\text{when }t\neq p\end{cases},\quad\forall\ j=1,...,d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have each term in <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cross</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i}=-{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j},\quad\langle{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\delta\mathbf{K}\rangle_{F}=-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot({\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{V}_{:,j}^{\top}{\mathbf{a}}_{i}=-{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j},\quad\langle{\bm{M}}^{(i,j)},\delta\mathbf{K}\rangle_{F}=-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot({\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting these two expressions back into Equation <a href="#A2.E28" title="In B.4 Joint-Pruning Score ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>, we obtain the cross term in closed form:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cross</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{d}}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot({\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{d}}\sum_{i=w}^{s}\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}\cdot({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})\cdot({\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{d}}\sum_{i=w}^{s}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot({\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top})\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐎</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{d}}\sum_{i=w}^{s}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot({\mathbf{q}}_{i}{\mathbf{k}}_{p}^{\top})\sum_{j=1}^{d}{\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}({\mathbf{V}}_{p,j}-{\mathbf{O}}_{i,j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boxed{2\sum_{i=w}^{s}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,p}\cdot(\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}\|^{2}_{2}-{\mathbf{v}}_{p}^{\top}{\mathbf{o}}_{i})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boxed{2\sum_{i=w}^{s}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,p}\cdot(\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}\|^{2}_{2}-{\mathbf{v}}_{p}^{\top}{\mathbf{o}}_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Finally, the saliency score of the token at position <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> when both value and key states are treated as pruning units is the summation of <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{value}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>value</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{value}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{key}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>key</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{key}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>cross</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}^{\text{cross}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{joint}}=2\sum_{i=w}^{s}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,p}\cdot(\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}\|^{2}_{2}-{\mathbf{v}}_{p}^{\top}{\mathbf{o}}_{i})+{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{value}}+{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{key}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>joint</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>value</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>key</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{joint}}=2\sum_{i=w}^{s}{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}^{2}\cdot{\mathbf{Z}}_{i,p}\cdot(\|{\mathbf{v}}_{p}\|^{2}_{2}-{\mathbf{v}}_{p}^{\top}{\mathbf{o}}_{i})+{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{value}}+{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{key}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p">This is consistent with the joint score expression in Equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> of Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Cache Pruning Scores ‣ 3 OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Reduction to Attention-Based Scores</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now show in detail that existing attention-based scores can be naturally recovered within our pruning framework. Suppose the pruning objective is defined over perturbations in the historical attention weights, <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}</annotation></semantics></math>, rather than in the attention outputs, <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{O}}_{w:s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐎</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{O}}_{w:s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, assume that each pruning unit corresponds to a single column of the attention matrix. Under these assumptions, minimizing the pruning-induced eviction error reduces to the following optimization problem:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\argmin_{p}\;\|\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}-{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}\|_{1,1}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\delta{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}\bm{e}_{p}+{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s,p}=\mathbf{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\argmin_{p}\;\|\widehat{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}-{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}\|_{1,1}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\delta{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s}\bm{e}_{p}+{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s,p}=\mathbf{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the entry-wise matrix <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm. In this case, the pruning constraint can be directly substituted into the objective, yielding the saliency score for token position <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{attn-based}}=\|{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s,p}\|_{1,1}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>attn-based</mtext></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{attn-based}}=\|{\mathbf{A}}_{w:s,p}\|_{1,1}=\sum_{i=w}^{s}|{\mathbf{A}}_{i,p}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This represents the <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm variant of our value-pruning score, <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{value}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>value</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{value}}</annotation></semantics></math>, but it excludes any value-state information. By varying the choice of the window index <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, the score <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{attn-based}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>attn-based</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{p}^{\text{attn-based}}</annotation></semantics></math> can flexibly target different perturbation windows, corresponding to various existing attention-based cache eviction strategies such as H<sub id="A2.SS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O, TOVA, and SnapKV.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Setup</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All the experiments are conducted on a single NVIDIA A100 GPU. We adapt the Hugging Face Transformers library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolf et al., 2020</a>)</cite> with PyTorch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al., 2019</a>)</cite> to implement the cache eviction algorithms. We use two representative instruction-tuned large language models as backbones: LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grattafiori et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and Qwen-2.5-7B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2023a</a>)</cite>. Both models employ Grouped Query Attention (GQA) and natively support a context window size of up to 128K tokens. All model inference is performed in half precision (bfloat16) with no quantization applied.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For tasks with extensive prefill prompt lengths, we use FlashAttention-2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao, 2023</a>)</cite> for prefill attention computation to reduce memory overhead. We then recompute attention weights for selected query positions as needed to compute saliency scores for token eviction, since attention weights are not materialized in FlashAttention.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Datasets</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> and existing cache eviction methods on three benchmarks: Needle-In-A-Haystack <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kamradt, 2023</a>)</cite>, LongBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>, and perplexity on the PG19 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rae et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, targeting prefill-phase static cache eviction and decoding-phase dynamic cache eviction, respectively.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Needle-In-A-Haystack (NIAH).</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the setup from the RULER benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hsieh et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, specifically the <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">niah_single_2</span> task<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2</span></span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA/RULER/blob/main/README.md" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/NVIDIA/RULER/blob/main/README.md</a></span></span></span>, where a randomly generated 7-digit “needle” passkey is embedded into a Paul Graham essay haystack. Context lengths of 4K, 8K, 16K, and 32K tokens are tested, with each setting containing 250 randomly generated samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LongBench.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LongBench includes 16 datasets across six task categories: single-document QA, multi-document QA, summarization, few-shot learning, synthetic reasoning, and code completion. The average input length is 6,711 words (approximately 16K tokens). For all models and methods, we truncate each sample to a maximum of 32K tokens. To ensure fair comparison, we follow SnapKV <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and perform cache eviction only during the prefill phase. Task-specific evaluation metrics (e.g., Exact Match/F1 for QA tasks, ROUGE for summarization tasks) are reported using LongBench’s official evaluation script<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3</span></span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://github.com/THUDM/LongBench/blob/main/LongBench/pred.py" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/THUDM/LongBench/blob/main/LongBench/pred.py</a></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Perplexity.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For decoding-phase cache eviction, we adopt the PG19 test set following the setup in StreamingLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. PG19 contains 100 full-length books, each averaging around 70K tokens. We evaluate on the standard test split<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4</span></span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/emozilla/pg19" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/emozilla/pg19</a></span></span></span> and compute perplexity across varying context lengths (from 1 to 32K), using a fixed KV cache budget of 1024 tokens for all dynamic cache eviction methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Baseline Setups</h3>

<section id="A3.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.1 </span>Prefill Eviction</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate baselines for prefill-phase cache eviction, we follow the experimental setup of SnapKV <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and perform cache eviction only during the prefill phase. Since SnapKV does not support eviction during decoding, no cached tokens are evicted in the decoding phase (for NIAH and LongBench tasks). In these benchmarks, the prompt length dominates and is the primary bottleneck; thus, applying decoding-phase eviction has little impact on performance.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">H<sub id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">H<sub id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O originally accumulates attention weights across all historical query positions to make eviction decisions. This is incompatible with the FlashAttention prefill implementation, as it requires recomputing full attention weights. To enable efficient implementation, we follow SnapKV’s version of H<sub id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O and accumulate query positions only within a recent perturbation window. For NIAH tasks, the perturbation window size is set to 16. For LongBench tasks, the window size is <math id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the prompt length <math id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>. All tokens in the perturbation window are treated as recent tokens, and the remaining cache budget is allocated to select heavy hitters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">TOVA.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TOVA does not accumulate attention weights but makes eviction decisions solely based on the most recent attention distribution. In all prefill-eviction evaluations, the cache budget is entirely allocated to the heavy hitters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SnapKV.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In SnapKV, the same perturbation window as in H<sub id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O is used. The key difference is that SnapKV additionally applies a max-pooling filter to the accumulated scores before eviction. For all SnapKV and <span id="A3.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span>-enhanced experiments, we follow the official implementation, using a max-pooling function with a kernel size of 7 and a stride of 1.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.2 </span>Decoding Eviction</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate baselines for decoding-phase cache eviction, we follow the setup of StreamingLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, where eviction decisions are made at every decoding step. All eviction methods are evaluated with a fixed 1024-token cache budget.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">StreamingLLM.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For StreamingLLM, we maintain the first 4 tokens as attention sinks and always keep the most recent 1020 tokens. Since attention sinks are essential for long-context generation, we retain the first 4 sink tokens in all other methods as well.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">H<sub id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each decoding step, H<sub id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O accumulates attention weights across all historical query positions to make eviction decisions. In all perplexity experiments of H<sub id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>O and its <span id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span>-enhanced variants, a 256-token recent window is always reserved. The remaining 764 tokens are dynamically selected using their respective saliency scores.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">TOVA.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As in prefill eviction, TOVA does not use a fixed recent window. All 1020 heavy-hitter tokens are dynamically selected based on the attention scores from the latest query position.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Implementation of OBCache</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a code implementation of <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> in pseudo PyTorch style, as illustrated in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix D Implementation of OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix D Implementation of OBCache ‣ OBCache: Optimal Brain KV Cache Pruning for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. These two algorithms demonstrate the computation of <span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OBCache</span> saliency scores and the cache eviction operation in the prefill phase.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
